// Liebestraum -- Franz Liszt
// Liebesträume, S. 541: No. 3 in A-flat major, "O lieb, so lang du lieben kannst"
//
// Performed and sequenced by Bernd Krueger, piano-midi.de (http://www.piano-midi.de).
// This score is an adaptation of that performance: its notes, dynamics, pedalling and
// tempo are transcribed from his MIDI file. Like the performance, it is licensed under
// the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Germany licence (CC BY-SA 3.0 DE):
// https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/de/ -- share it and adapt it, with
// this credit, under the same licence. The composition itself is in the public domain.
//
// A song without words in three verses, each wider than the last, joined by two
// cadenzas: the melody sits in the middle of the texture with the arpeggios
// shared by both hands around it. Bar 0 is the pickup; the cadenza bars are
// longer (12/4 and 8/4), so some sections are fractional 6/4 bars.
//
// Reading it: one modelled grand plays the note lists below, merged. An entry is
// [beat note dur vel]: beats are quarter notes from the start, dur in quarters, vel
// the key's velocity 0..1. Each bar's comment names its dynamic (pp < 0.31 <= p <
// 0.44 <= mp < 0.57 <= mf < 0.69 <= f < 0.82 <= ff). [beat @pedal 1] puts the sustain
// pedal down, [beat @pedal 0] lifts it. Each Section's `tempo` is the performer's
// rubato: [beat bpm] from the section's first beat, held to the next point.
use mod.score.*

